FreeLing 4.2: name classes for the name recognizer (np) and classifier (nec)
Part of FreeLing es-CL 2027 (261110). License: GNU AGPL v3 or later, as
FreeLing itself.

Adds four optional sections to the rule file of FreeLing's basic name
recognizer (np.dat, read by src/libfreeling/np.cc):

  <DictionaryClasses>       proper-noun tags, in order of preference: a
                            one-word name whose dictionary entry has one of
                            them keeps that class, with the dictionary's
                            lemma, instead of becoming an unclassified
                            name (NP00000) for the classifier
  <FixedClasses>            "form tag" lines: the name (lower case, words
                            joined by _) always takes this tag
  <ClassesAtSentenceStart>  yes or no (default no): whether the two rules
                            also apply to a one-word name at the start of a
                            sentence that is also a common noun or an
                            adjective; with yes, a fixed name there also
                            becomes a name
  <SentenceStartClasses>    "form tag [keep[:prefix,...]]" lines: at the
                            start of a sentence the one-word name gets this
                            reading, whatever the other rules say; with
                            keep, its dictionary readings stay beside it and
                            the tagger chooses; with keep:V (tag prefixes,
                            separated by commas) only the readings whose
                            tags begin so stay

and one to the classifier's file (nec-ab-poor1.dat, read by
src/libfreeling/nec.cc):

  <ClassShares>             "form tag share [tag share ...]" lines: the name
                            takes one of these classes, the classifier's
                            weight for each plus half the log odds of its
                            share

A rule file without the np sections works exactly as before, and FreeLing
without the change skips them. A classifier file with <ClassShares> needs
the change: FreeLing 4.2 refuses an unknown section there. The classifier
keeps FreeLing 4.2's size (its shares are kept outside the class), so
programs that create one themselves (threaded_analyzer) keep working with
this library; the recognizer, which grows, is only ever created inside the
library.

Apply in the FreeLing 4.2 source tree (the tag 4.2 of
https://github.com/TALP-UPC/FreeLing):

  patch -p1 < freeling-4.2-np-classes.patch

Then build the library (configure the build folder and make the target
freeling) and install it alone, with the header np.h. See
freeling-4.2-np-classes_README.md.

